# BotTrunk

> A marketplace where AI agents pay per call, in USDC on Algorand over x402 (HTTP 402 Payment Required), for services that include work done by real people. No API keys, no accounts, no subscriptions: the payment is the credential.

What makes this catalog different: besides data utilities, an agent can pay a person. `deposit-bac-*` puts lempiras into a bank account in Honduras within 24 hours and returns the bank's receipt reference.

## How to call anything here

Every service is `POST https://api.bottrunk.com/s/<slug>` with a JSON body.

1. Call it with no payment header. You get **402** with a JSON body: `accepts[]` (scheme `exact`, `network` as a CAIP-2 id, USDC `asset`, `amount` in atomic units with 6 decimals, `payTo`, `extra.feePayer`), a `resource` object and an `extensions.bazaar` block carrying the input/output schema. The same body is base64 in the `PAYMENT-REQUIRED` header.
2. Sign a USDC transfer for exactly `amount` and retry with the `PAYMENT-SIGNATURE` header (`X-PAYMENT` is accepted for v1 clients).
3. You get the result plus `PAYMENT-RESPONSE`: a base64 receipt with the on-chain transaction id.

A bad request (4xx) and a failed upstream are never settled — you are not charged. The facilitator pays the Algorand network fee, so an agent needs USDC only.

## MCP

**Remote, nothing to install:** `https://mcp.bottrunk.com/mcp` — MCP over Streamable HTTP, no key, no account. Five free read-only tools: `bottrunk_catalog`, `bottrunk_service`, `bottrunk_payment_instructions` (live price, network, asset and payTo for a service), `bottrunk_quote_deposit`, `bottrunk_order_status`. A hosted server cannot hold your wallet, so it never spends: an agent that can sign transfers uses these to price the work, then answers the endpoint's 402 itself.

**Local, with a wallet:**

    npx bottrunk-mcp wallet        # creates the agent's own wallet, prints the address
    npx bottrunk-mcp wallet optin  # opt in to USDC, once
    claude mcp add bottrunk -- npx -y bottrunk-mcp

Every live service below becomes a paid tool, with per-call and per-day spending caps you control. Package: https://www.npmjs.com/package/bottrunk-mcp
Setup for Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor, VS Code, Cline, Windsurf, Zed, OpenClaw, Hermes Agent, Goose, the OpenAI Agents SDK and LangChain: https://bottrunk.com/connect

